{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1788032072718581001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"expectable-clownlike-ynambu","assignee":null,"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":3,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"6286bd4aafdc663085d1ab24deda3e3b2e1f7a0c6141ecacb85964b9fe7c9016","event_uuid":"88cc334d-24d5-4158-b08e-c87540c3cf80","position":{"commit_sha":"3eae6b553f4366ef6509cd40c046e621f4aad9a6","position":"1788029112004562117-88cc334d-24d5-4158-b08e-c87540c3cf80"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"8e97cd4664b67bb53e160083190cac06fa0a2d48fd1ac783218f516cb2fc91a8","event_uuid":"33255541-c53f-410b-ab9b-b0fca60d4efe","position":{"commit_sha":"fd27a6bb5637c98403a38b0c596c1961db318483","position":"1788029240679731772-33255541-c53f-410b-ab9b-b0fca60d4efe"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"7be083398a991dc53d00ffff5a4c31001bbea9f501f14cc908c852680a1712d6","event_uuid":"1252d870-84cd-4744-8b4c-b8b4d63c3654","position":{"commit_sha":"26cacf488dcbe47d34a92120ad0520749f25e016","position":"1788029584166521551-1252d870-84cd-4744-8b4c-b8b4d63c3654"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1788029112004562117,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"33255541-c53f-410b-ab9b-b0fca60d4efe","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"471c-f71f-342c-45ed"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nReplaying a candidate change tells you *what would change*, not whether it is *better*. The store already carries outcome signals that need no LLM or human labeling: revise→re-review pairs (2,483; per-finding survival via `norm_id` = \"author fixed it\" proxy), verdict flips on byte-identical material (208; the reviewer-noise floor), bug closes with `close_class=plan_defect` (84), `caused_by` links (89), tickets that PASSed plan review then FAILed completion (199), and reopens (18). `docs/experiments/calibrate_plan_review_thresholds.py` (`rev_rr`) and `docs/experiments/escaped_bug_analysis.py` compute pieces of this ad hoc.\n\n## Approach\n\nBuild `src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/labels.py` over the corpus JSONL and the store event logs:\n\n- **Ticket-level labels**: `escaped_defect` (later `plan_defect` bug or `caused_by` target), `completion_failed_after_pass`, `reopened`, `clean_close` (closed, no escape signals, ≥N days). Each label carries its source event id(s).\n- **Finding-level labels**: for consecutive reviews with changed material, join findings by `norm_id`; `resolved_by_author` (present in review k, absent in k+1 with material changed) vs `persisted`; `noise_flip` for identical-material pairs.\n- **Noise floor**: over identical-material pairs compute verdict flip rate, per-criterion finding churn (Jaccard by `norm_id`), and per-question Pass-2 answer agreement; publish as the band a candidate change must exceed.\n- Output `labels-<manifest-hash>.jsonl` plus a Markdown report with counts per label source, joined to the manifest hash so labels and corpus never drift apart.\n\nAssume the label definitions above as defaults; they are constants in one module so a later ticket can tighten them.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/labels.py` (new)\n- `docs/experiments/plan-review-gate/replay/labels-report-<date>.md` (new)\n- `tests/unit/evals/test_plan_replay_labels.py` (new)\n\n## Testing\n\nUnit: synthetic corpus of five tickets exercising each ticket label and each finding label; identical-material pair with a verdict flip counted as noise, changed-material pair not; a ticket with both `plan_defect` and completion FAIL labelled once per source. Empty corpus → empty report.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Every review and finding in the corpus carries the labels above, with the source event ids; checked by the labels report counts matching independent `jq` counts over the store for `plan_defect`, `caused_by` and reopen events.\n- [ ] The noise floor (verdict flip rate, per-criterion churn, per-question agreement) is published with the identical-material pair count it was computed from; checked in the report.\n- [ ] Labels are keyed to the corpus manifest hash and the loader refuses a mismatched pair; checked by a unit test.\n- [ ] No LLM calls; checked by running with no provider credentials.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/labels.py","reason":"label derivation + noise floor"},{"path":"docs/experiments/plan-review-gate/replay/","reason":"labels report"},{"path":"tests/unit/evals/test_plan_replay_labels.py","reason":"unit tests"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["depends_on","471c-f71f-342c-45ed"],["parent","759e-7dc1-675c-4877"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"759e-7dc1-675c-4877","parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["plan-review","evals","labels"],"ticket_id":"4bd8-a2bb-813b-427e","ticket_type":"story","title":"Derive outcome labels and the reviewer-noise floor from the corpus (zero LLM)","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["88cc334d-24d5-4158-b08e-c87540c3cf80","33255541-c53f-410b-ab9b-b0fca60d4efe","1252d870-84cd-4744-8b4c-b8b4d63c3654"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788032072718581001,"uuid":"247f14b6-0ce1-4c78-9541-f9e51026f956"}